post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> As a system service, as the user trunk, with the data in /var/lib/trunk:
      sudo -u trunk trunk user add NAME -admin -data /var/lib/trunk
      sudo systemctl enable --now trunk
    It listens on 127.0.0.1:8420; /usr/share/doc/trunk-photos/Caddyfile puts it behind Caddy.
==> Or as your own user, with the data in ~/.local/share/trunk:
      systemctl --user enable --now trunk
      trunk user add NAME -admin -data ~/.local/share/trunk
==> trunk-ai (content search, faces) needs onnxruntime; see trunk-ai.service in
    /usr/lib/systemd/system/ or /usr/lib/systemd/user/.
MSG
}
